<title>UK: Christian Salvesen H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Christian Salvesen H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		12.30		  vs 10.84</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.80		   vs up 0.3</p>
<p> Pretax		     51.6		   vs 45.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   383.1		  vs 345.9</p>
<p> Combined div (pence)   20.8		   vs3.5</p>
<p> Operating profit	 53.7		   vs 45.4</p>
<p> Tax			  15.7		   vs 13.5</p>
<p> Retained profit	  25.2		   vs 21.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 3, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Dec 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Transport and sevices firm Christian Salvesen Plc said the combined dividend was the interim dividend payment plus a special dividend totalling 150 million stg.</p>
<p>It also announced it is to demerge its hire unit, three months after rejecting a hostile takeover.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
